    legal:`THINGDADDY SOFTWARE AND FIRMWARE WARRANTY

1. IDENTITY BINDING. This Software Warranty is bound to: (a) TD:GIAI — the specific physical device instance running this software; (b) TD:GMN — the model/firmware version cohort; (c) TD:GDTI — this Warranty document. Software versions are identified by their GMN identity in the ThingDaddy registry.

2. SOFTWARE DEFECT REMEDY. Manufacturer will provide: (a) bug fixes addressing material non-conformance with published specifications; (b) security patches for vulnerabilities identified by CVE; (c) firmware updates maintaining SiLA 2 protocol compliance. All updates are identified by new GMN versions and recorded as EPCIS Object Events.

3. SUPPORT LIFECYCLE. Software support follows the GMN version lifecycle: Active Support (full warranty), Maintenance Mode (security only), End of Life (no support). Version status is queryable in the ThingDaddy directory for the device model (GMN).`,
